---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { getContracts } from '../site/contracts';
// `.card`, `.card-top`, `.per`, `.stamp`, `.off-note`, `.silent` and the
// `.cons` rules are all in chain.css — imported here for the same reason every
// other route imports the styles it renders (see the note in WorkMeter.astro),
// so this page cannot ship unstyled. `.page-head` lives in base.css, which
// `Base.astro` always loads.
import '../styles/chain.css';

/**
 * §6 — the author's projects, presented as deployed contracts.
 *
 * §5.1 governs this page and says so by name: `content/contracts/` is read at
 * build time and hashed nowhere, and "anything not on the chain must say so
 * where it is displayed", using the vocabulary the site already has rather than
 * a third formulation. So this is the mempool's card, verbatim — the dashed
 * `.card.offchain`, the `.stamp.off` badge, an `.off-note` whose own words are
 * `chưa lên chuỗi` — because a project is off the chain in exactly the sense a
 * draft is, and the reader has already met that treatment on `/mempool` and on
 * `/about`.
 *
 * The one thing this page must not do is call a contract **verified**. §6's
 * phrase is "projects as verified contracts, source linked to GitHub", and on a
 * real explorer that word is a check anyone can rerun: published source against
 * deployed bytecode. Here the source is a url this build never fetches, to a
 * repository that can change tomorrow. Nothing on this site verifies it, so the
 * note says the opposite in as many words — see `src/site/contracts.ts` for the
 * full reasoning and why `Contract` carries no such field to print.
 *
 * The empty list is the ordinary state, not an edge case: `content/contracts/`
 * ships empty. It gets a sentence of its own rather than a blank card, so the
 * page reads as "nothing has been published here yet" instead of as a page that
 * failed to load.
 *
 * No clock (§14): `getContracts()` reads a directory.
 */
const contracts = getContracts();
---

<Base
  title="Contracts — Blogchain"
  description="Các dự án của tác giả — đọc lúc build, nằm ngoài chuỗi."
>
  <div class="page-head">
    <h1>Contracts</h1>
    <span class="sub"><span class="num">{contracts.length}</span> dự án</span>
  </div>

  <article class="card offchain" aria-label="Contracts">
    <div class="card-top">
      <span class="per">Dự án</span>
      <span class="stamp off">Ngoài chuỗi</span>
    </div>
    <p class="off-note">
      Đây là các dự án của tác giả, <strong>chưa lên chuỗi</strong>: không có hash, không có địa chỉ,
      không có gas, không thuộc khối nào. Chuỗi không biết gì về chúng. Liên kết mã nguồn cũng chỉ
      là một đường dẫn ra ngoài — trang này <strong>không kiểm chứng được</strong> thứ nằm ở đầu
      kia, và kho mã ấy có thể đổi bất cứ lúc nào. Thứ trang này kiểm chứng được nằm ở <a href="/blocks">Blocks</a> và <a href="/tx">Transactions</a>.
    </p>
    {contracts.length > 0 ? (
      <ul class="cons">
        {contracts.map((contract) => (
          <li>
            {/* `encodeURIComponent`, because a contract's slug is a filename
                the author chose — `content/contracts/máy chủ mcp.md` is an
                ordinary thing to write, and it is the first slug on this site
                that is freeform prose rather than a `YYYY-MM-DD-` post name.
                Unencoded it renders `href="/contract/máy chủ & mcp"`, which is
                a url no browser resolves to the page the build wrote beside it,
                and which this site's own dead-link check reports as never
                built. One segment, so `encodeURIComponent` and not `encodeURI`:
                a `/` or a `?` in a filename is part of the name, not structure.
                The route param stays raw — `getStaticPaths` writes the
                directory, and a static host decodes the request back to it. */}
            <h2 class="t"><a href={`/contract/${encodeURIComponent(contract.slug)}`}>{contract.name}</a></h2>
            {contract.summary === '' ? null : <p class="s">{contract.summary}</p>}
            <span class="g">
              {contract.language ?? '—'}
              {' · '}
              {/* No anchor at all when there is no url — never a placeholder
                  href. The site links only to what exists, the same rule
                  `/about` puts an unfilled profile link under, and the em dash
                  the mempool already uses for a field that does not exist. */}
              {contract.repo === null
                ? '— chưa công bố mã nguồn'
                : <a href={contract.repo}>Source</a>}
            </span>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ul>
    ) : (
      <p class="silent">Chưa có hợp đồng nào được công bố ở đây.</p>
    )}
  </article>
</Base>
